WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:07.520
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:15.620
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.660
So won't you come with me?

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.760
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.930
And every moment by moment

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.390
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.850
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.270
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.940
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.700
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.240
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.710
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:09.340
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.260
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.260
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.730
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.490
Fools! You are guns who have lost your true form.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.490
You have no reason to exist.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.620
What?!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.790
You cannot run.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.620
Either we win, or you win.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.420
We'll decide this right here.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.280
There they are!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.490
I won't forgive them!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.660
I'll never forgive them!

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.870
Damn them!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.540
We're not gonna lose to some cardboard car!

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.510
They rolled over.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.170
Let's capture them and interrogate them!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.720
Jeez, this sucks!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.930
But we have an idea of where they're going now.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.060
Their plan is to make us fight them in the shopping district next to the train station.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.190
We'll split into two groups and trap them from either side of the station!

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.360
Fukko, you two approach from the Ginza side.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:06.960
<i>Pests...</i>

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.540
I'll back you up, so you approach from the left,

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.100
circle around them, and provide covering fire from there.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.000
Go!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.690
It's begun.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.690
We need to hurry, too.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:42.420
Sixteen!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:47.960
Damn it.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.370
You okay?

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.500
Yeah. I lost a magazine, though.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.090
That was a shotgun just now, wasn't it?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.220
And one that uses magazines at that...

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.420
That was a Saiga.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.340
I knew it...

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.100
I believe that's the one developed by the Russian company, Izhmash...

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.850
That's right.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:10.100
The shotgun was originally made for slugs designed for hunting,

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.440
but given its destructive power at close range,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.300
it started being used for destroying doors and riot suppression.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.940
Shotgun shells are containers that hold many smaller bullets, and they're loaded

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.920
one by one into a tube magazine by hand.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:27.340
This means reloading takes a considerable amount of time.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.860
So, the attraction of the Saiga is

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:43.460
that it uses a box magazine to reduce reload times to practically zero.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.580
<i>These girls are going to be a bit tough.</i>

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.230
<i>She's running away when I swap magazines.</i>

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.580
<i>I wonder if Elle-chan is gonna make it in time.</i>

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.450
You're a goner.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:49.870
Elle-chan, over here!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.880
Are you okay?

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.960
Did your magazine catch get warped?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.220
So you're gonna throw up your magazine...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.480
At this rate, we're gonna be the ones trapped in the middle.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.390
We need to do something about the person behind us first.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:19.600
Elle-chan, you take a rest. I'll figure something out.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.760
What are you trying to pull?!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.550
You don't even have a magazine!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.560
You little smart a—

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:02.690
She used her knees to hold the magazine in place...

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.490
Crap! We can't get through here!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:19.040
It might be best to retreat for now.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.960
Damn it. They've got us on either side.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.800
This is not the time...

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:31.760
Sixteen!

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.010
What now?!

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.400
You did it?

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.020
It wasn't me.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.980
That's not all of them.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:47.730
Sako!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.240
Galil told me what was going on.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.240
She said she smelled an AK.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:53.530
So, when she was...

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.030
She was talking to you?

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.370
The ones who were making the most racket seem to have left.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:05.040
Did you know this was going to happen?!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.050
I noticed some weird things going on awhile ago.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.800
How come you didn't tell us sooner?!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.930
Didn't I leave Galil here?

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.390
A lot of good that does us!

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.300
What was that?!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.510
Sixteen!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:25.940
But I didn't think they'd make this into such a big event.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.820
What are they after?

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.190
"After?"

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:30.990
They're not "after" anything.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.190
What did you say?!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.110
If I had to guess,

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.570
I'd say they're just looking for a good fight.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.740
What the hell?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.410
That's why they're doing this?

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:49.710
Funko-chan?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.760
I don't hear Fukko anymore.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.920
Sorry, but you two handle the others on your own!

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.550
Sig!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.310
There're still some of 'em left!

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.140
I'll back you up. Let's go for it.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.730
That was the plan all along.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.370
Funko-chan?

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.010
Funko-chan!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.890
No, she's a fake!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.060
Roger that.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.530
Now we don't have to worry about the brains anymore.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.350
So hot...

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.700
<i>My barrel's overheating, so my grouping's all messed up.</i>

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.500
<i>I bet he'd get mad if he saw me like this.</i>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:41.950
<i>Sensei always treats us like girls.</i>

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.350
<i>Not that I don't like that about him.</i>

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.680
<i>They know we're coming, right?</i>

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.340
<i>Five of them left.</i>

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:45.050
<i>I'm not sure this'll go well, but I've got to do it.</i>

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.670
She's up there!

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.240
You're not getting away from me!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.760
Close range battles are fun.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.430
You can see how scared your opponent is!

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.350
You can't see someone who's hiding!

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.730
There's nothing you can do!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.330
We're so close to the shopping district!

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.540
This is tough...

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:01.630
We can't do anything when they have so much distance on their side.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.720
There's one way.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.510
What's that?

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.640
This!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.140
Is that something a leader's supposed to do?!

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.560
I told you before! I don't remember becoming everyone's leader!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.190
I knew it! I should've taken over!

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.740
Shut up! Like that'd ever happen.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.860
I'd be way better than you!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.930
If you want this to end, just give it up.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:56.690
Say, "We've lost. Please forgive us."

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.900
What the hell?

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.770
Yeah, right!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.690
Damn it!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.350
Hm...

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.830
How unexpected...

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:22.820
What is it?

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.800
I almost had her.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.590
<i>That's enough.</i>

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.590
<i>I want you to go over to where Saiga's</i>

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:30.760
<i>fighting that girl who speaks in the Kansai dialect.</i>

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.600
Huh? What the hell?

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:33.810
Are you stupid?!

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.310
<i>That's an order.</i>

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.530
<i>Hurry up.</i>

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.860
Damn it!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.820
What's going on?

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.950
Right.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.210
I understand.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.960
Right. Right.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.460
Roger that.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:30.280
Sig.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.160
How could I have fallen for that?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.530
Thank you, Elle.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.960
Where are you shooting?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.540
They can't see me.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:31.970
The... idiot... needs... to... die.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.090
The idiot needs to die?!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:34.590
What the hell?

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.890
Fine, then!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.540
AK die, huh?

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.700
How funny.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.040
Stop joking around!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.960
What are you thinking?

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.790
The look in your eyes has improved,

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.040
but it's still not quite there yet.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:09.880
How about this, then?

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:17.840
Elle-chan!

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.010
Damn her!

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:23.980
Sig-chan!

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.190
This isn't any better!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.030
Just shoot!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.490
Reinforcements!

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:40.240
You've caused so much destruction throughout the town and hurt the people I love!

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.620
We won't forgive you!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.290
I like that look in your eyes!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.590
That's the look I've been waiting for!

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:09.860
Stop this!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.360
Sensei!

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.740
A human?

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:19.320
Damn.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.820
Sensei!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.830
Hold on, Sensei!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.580
You were hit?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.000
Stop it...

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.250
Stop this ridiculous game.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.710
Game?!

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.800
Sensei! Sensei!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.560
I-It's a good thing...

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.770
It's a good thing we're guns.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.650
As long as you're not shot by another human,

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:54.020
you won't die from one of our bullets.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.190
I... I see.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.280
It's a good thing?

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:01.110
Screw this!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.250
Yes!

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.620
That's it!

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.120
That's the look.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.460
That's how you're supposed to look.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.500
Go ahead and fire.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.210
And then finish me off.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.590
Everything'll start from there.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:26.100
If you're going to hesitate, then I'll shoot.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:30.810
FNC!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.820
Why's a human getting in the way?

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.370
Do you have the right to tell us to stop

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.580
when you're the ones producing us?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.330
That's exactly why I'm telling you to stop.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:54.170
But we won't change the way we live.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.340
That's because humans wished for this.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.220
Our paradise will come.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.220
Sig!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.590
It will.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.140
Let's go.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:16.270
That's not true.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.570
We...

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:58.150
They've changed a little since that incident.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:04.490
I think they understood what's most important for us guns.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.990
I think they've grown a little.

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.780
Yeah.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:12.290
At the rate they're going, I'm sure they'll...

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.410
Huh? They haven't changed.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.330
Sixteen hasn't gotten any taller.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.880
G Cutie...

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:19.750
Huh?

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.760
I think you need to start growing.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.260
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.260
They got to meet someone good.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.100
Yeah.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.930
I just ate some good meat, too.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.770
It was worth the effort to get him to come here.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.370
Yeah.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:42.030
I'm sure he was really surprised about a lot of things, but I'm glad.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.320
SG550.

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:44.950
Here.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:45.740
FNC.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.240
Here.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.660
M16A4.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:48.370
Right on.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:49.910
L85A1.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.030
Here.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.040
You guys'll be taking your high school entrance exams soon.

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:55.580
Work hard.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.130
Oh, we don't have anything like that, Sensei.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.000
Huh? You don't?

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.670
We're assault rifles.

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:07.630
We can't turn into battle rifles!

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:17.100
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:24.650
Together we braved

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:36.580
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:44.210
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:49.840
When I ran

00:22:52.720 --> 00:23:03.230
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:10.950
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:18.120
Something is bound to change

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:26.300
One by one the days I tore off pile up

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:30.180
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:36.350
They will be my strength for days to come
